I’ve verified that the attribution control is currently gathering attributions from every sub‐layer regardless of its parent group’s visibility. Internally it does:

```js
this.getMap()
  .getAllLayers()
  .flatMap(layer => layer.getAttributions(frameState))
```

but each layer’s own `.getVisible()` flag is true, so it still reports its attribution even though the group above it is invisible. The rendering engine already maintains a flattened `frameState.layerStatesArray` with an accurate `.visible` boolean that respects both the layer’s and any parent group’s visibility. We can simply pull only those layer‐states where `visible === true` and then ask each layer for its attributions.

Below is a single *SEARCH/REPLACE* patch in `src/ol/control/Attribution.js` that replaces the old `getAllLayers()`–based gatherer with one based on `frameState.layerStatesArray`. It only returns attributions for actually showing (visible) layers:

```javascript
